From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:36:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] Review of final3: the kept index's contract stated
 exactly, and a witness for fix 2's suppression

Comment and test only; the binary is unchanged.

cmd/restic/wait_index_load.go said that with any backend this build knows
what stock knows at each point. That is more than the code does. The index
read during the lock wait is validated by a listing, name and size, taken
where stock lists; it is not validated by reading the files again. On a
backend whose listing can still show a file after it was deleted, an index
file removed by a concurrent prune is not noticed when its content was read
during the wait. Stock notices it only without a copy of the file in its
local cache; with the cached copy, the default, it behaves as this build.

TestAsyncSaveResultSuppressionIsNarrow is the reviewer's witness for red
team fix 2: a save's error is withheld from the uploader's group only on a
repack's context that is cancelled, and reported on every other context.
It catches the two mutations of fix 2 that the tests did not catch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
